* ============================================================================
* workspace_multi_demo.dts
*
* MULTIPLE WORKSPACES -- A GUIDED TOUR. THIS IS NOT A TEST.
*
* WHAT THIS IS
*   A narrated walkthrough of the multi-workspace surface: NEW, UNDER, SWITCH,
*   REGISTRY, SET RECURSION, scoped CLOSE, and what happens when one file is
*   open in more than one workspace. Every step prints what it is about to do
*   and then shows the registry, so the output reads top to bottom as an
*   explanation rather than as a log.
*
* WHAT THIS IS NOT, AND WHY THE DISTINCTION IS ENFORCED HERE
*   It asserts NOTHING. There are no markers, no .T./.F. lines, and no name in
*   this file resembles a test id. That is deliberate: a demo that also carries
*   assertions is a test that nobody maintains, and a green from it would be
*   read as evidence when it was only narration.
*
*   The regression that DOES gate this behaviour is
*   workspace_multi_regression.dts. If you want to know whether multiple
*   workspaces still work, run that. If you want to know what they DO, run
*   this.
*
* THE SURFACE THIS TOUR COVERS, AND WHERE IT IS OTHERWISE UNDOCUMENTED
*   WORKSPACE NEW / UNDER / SWITCH / REGISTRY / CLOSE ALL and SET RECURSION are
*   all implemented, and as of 2026-08-22 NONE of them appear in the
*   @dottalk.usage contract block in src/cli/cmd_workspace.cpp. WORKSPACE USAGE
*   will not show you a single verb this file uses. Until that contract is
*   refreshed, this tour is the usage documentation.
*
* THE THREE LINES IN THIS FILE THAT CAN VANISH, AND WHY THEY ARE PAIRED
*   88 of the 91 ? lines here are string literals: they cannot error, so they
*   always print. Exactly THREE read a field, and a read that errors PRINTS
*   NOTHING rather than failing -- the same evaluator behaviour the regression
*   header records.
*
*   In a regression that is survivable, because a missing marker name is
*   conspicuous in the results. In a narrated tour it is not: one line missing
*   from forty is invisible, and the demo would read as complete while having
*   silently skipped the only place it shows live data.
*
*   So each of the three is preceded by a LITERAL line naming what it expects.
*   If the read vanishes, the expectation dangles with no partner and the gap
*   is obvious. Added 2026-08-22 after mutation-testing the regression made the
*   failure mode concrete.
*
* RUN
*   ./datarun.ps1 -CommandLines 'DO scripts\workspace_multi_demo.dts'
*
*   Paths given to DO resolve against the DATA ROOT, not the repo root.
*   Run it ONCE per process: workspace names cannot be reclaimed in a session
*   (see ACT 6), so a second run in the same session will refuse the NEWs.
* ============================================================================

SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX

FORMULA "WORKSPACE-MULTI-DEMO-BEGIN"

SET RECURSION ON
WORKSPACE SWITCH DEFAULT
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
ERASE demodef CONFIRM
ERASE demoa CONFIRM
ERASE demoa1 CONFIRM
ERASE demob CONFIRM
ERASE demob1 CONFIRM
ERASE demoshare CONFIRM

? " "
? "=========================================================================="
? "ACT 1 -- A workspace is a NAMED GROUP OF WORK AREAS."
? "=========================================================================="
? "You always start in one. It is called DEFAULT and you did not create it."
? "Opening a table right now puts that area into DEFAULT's group."
? " "

SELECT 0
CREATE X64 DEMODEF (ID N(4), MARK C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 1
REPLACE MARK WITH "DEF"

SELECT 7
CREATE X64 DEMOSHARE (ID N(4), MARK C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 9
REPLACE MARK WITH "SHARE"

? " "
? "Two areas now belong to DEFAULT. The registry is the authority on that:"
WORKSPACE REGISTRY

? " "
? "=========================================================================="
? "ACT 2 -- NEW creates a workspace. UNDER nests one inside another."
? "=========================================================================="
? "Names are how a person refers to a workspace, so they must be unique."
? "Two trees are built here so both RECURSION arms can be shown later."
? " "

WORKSPACE NEW WSDEMO_A
WORKSPACE NEW WSDEMO_A1 UNDER WSDEMO_A
WORKSPACE NEW WSDEMO_B
WORKSPACE NEW WSDEMO_B1 UNDER WSDEMO_B

? " "
? "Note the depth column: A1 and B1 report depth 1 and name their parent."
? "Note also that all four have ZERO members. Creating a workspace does not"
? "move anything into it -- only opening an area while it is CURRENT does."
WORKSPACE REGISTRY

? " "
? "=========================================================================="
? "ACT 3 -- SWITCH decides which workspace the NEXT area joins."
? "=========================================================================="
? "This is the whole mental model. SWITCH, then open. Not the reverse."
? " "

WORKSPACE SWITCH WSDEMO_A
SELECT 1
CREATE X64 DEMOA (ID N(4), MARK C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 2
REPLACE MARK WITH "A"

WORKSPACE SWITCH WSDEMO_A1
SELECT 2
CREATE X64 DEMOA1 (ID N(4), MARK C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 3
REPLACE MARK WITH "A1"

WORKSPACE SWITCH WSDEMO_B
SELECT 3
CREATE X64 DEMOB (ID N(4), MARK C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 4
REPLACE MARK WITH "B"

WORKSPACE SWITCH WSDEMO_B1
SELECT 4
CREATE X64 DEMOB1 (ID N(4), MARK C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 5
REPLACE MARK WITH "B1"

? " "
? "Each workspace now owns exactly the area opened while it was current:"
WORKSPACE REGISTRY

? " "
? "=========================================================================="
? "ACT 4 -- ONE FILE, THREE WORKSPACES. This is where AGAIN matters."
? "=========================================================================="
? "DEMOSHARE.DBF is already open in DEFAULT, area 7."
? "A bare USE would be REFUSED: the engine will not silently give you a second"
? "handle on a file you already hold. AGAIN is the explicit way to ask."
? "Watch the alias: the engine auto-names the extra instances and SAYS SO."
? " "

WORKSPACE SWITCH WSDEMO_A
SELECT 5
USE demoshare AGAIN

WORKSPACE SWITCH WSDEMO_B
SELECT 6
USE demoshare AGAIN

? " "
? "One file, three work areas, three different owners. This is the case that"
? "separates a per-workspace area registry from a global one:"
WORKSPACE REGISTRY

? " "
? "=========================================================================="
? "ACT 5 -- CLOSE is SCOPED, and RECURSION decides how far it reaches."
? "=========================================================================="
? "With RECURSION ON, closing A also closes its child A1."
? "Everything outside that subtree -- DEFAULT, B, B1 -- is untouched,"
? "INCLUDING B's own handle on the shared file."
? " "

SET RECURSION ON
WORKSPACE SWITCH WSDEMO_A
WORKSPACE CLOSE

? " "
? "A and A1 are now at members 0. B, B1 and DEFAULT are exactly as they were:"
WORKSPACE REGISTRY

? " "
? "Proof by reading rather than by claiming: B's tables still answer."
WORKSPACE SWITCH WSDEMO_B
SELECT 3
GO TOP
? "  DEMOB  expected B      -- the NEXT line is the live read:"
? "  DEMOB  actual        : " + ALLTRIM(MARK)
SELECT 6
GO TOP
? "  shared expected SHARE  -- the NEXT line is the live read:"
? "  shared actual        : " + ALLTRIM(MARK)

? " "
? "Now the contrast. With RECURSION OFF, closing B does NOT descend into B1."
? "The flag does not gate whether nesting may EXIST -- it gates whether an"
? "operation DESCENDS. B1 stays open and readable."
? " "

SET RECURSION OFF
WORKSPACE SWITCH WSDEMO_B
WORKSPACE CLOSE

WORKSPACE REGISTRY

? " "
? "B1 survived its parent being closed, because RECURSION was OFF:"
WORKSPACE SWITCH WSDEMO_B1
SELECT 4
GO TOP
? "  DEMOB1 expected B1     -- the NEXT line is the live read:"
? "  DEMOB1 actual        : " + ALLTRIM(MARK)

? " "
? "=========================================================================="
? "ACT 6 -- THE LIMITS. Two of them, and the engine tells you about one."
? "=========================================================================="
? " "
? "LIMIT 1 -- relations are cleared GLOBALLY on a scoped close."
? "  The relation graph is not workspace-scoped yet, so closing one workspace"
? "  clears relations belonging to areas that are still open elsewhere. The"
? "  engine prints that warning itself, naming the count, rather than doing it"
? "  quietly. It is an AIF-078 stage 3 limitation, not a defect in your script."
? " "
? "LIMIT 2 -- a workspace NAME cannot be reclaimed within a session."
? "  WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL releases every area everywhere, and after it the"
? "  registry STILL lists every workspace at members 0. There is no DROP,"
? "  DELETE or REMOVE verb. Try WORKSPACE NEW WSDEMO_A again after the"
? "  teardown below and it will refuse. That is why this file says run it"
? "  once per process."
? " "

SET RECURSION ON
WORKSPACE SWITCH DEFAULT
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL

? " "
? "After CLOSE ALL: zero members everywhere, but FIVE workspaces still named."
? "  Five, not four: DEFAULT counts. It is the workspace ACT 1 pointed out you"
? "  were already standing in, and CLOSE ALL empties it like any other."
WORKSPACE REGISTRY

ERASE demodef CONFIRM
ERASE demoa CONFIRM
ERASE demoa1 CONFIRM
ERASE demob CONFIRM
ERASE demob1 CONFIRM
ERASE demoshare CONFIRM

? " "
? "=========================================================================="
? "END OF TOUR."
? "  The gating regression is scripts\workspace_multi_regression.dts."
? "  This file proved nothing and was not trying to."
? "=========================================================================="

FORMULA "WORKSPACE-MULTI-DEMO-END"
